window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-cb94fa07f6e7450c"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"run-codex-security-in-github-actions\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"github-actions-codex-security\">在 GitHub Actions 中运行 Codex Security</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>在 GitHub Actions 中运行 Codex Security，可以检查拉取请求中的变更，或按计划扫描代码仓库。Action 会安装 CLI、保存结构化报告，并生成作业摘要和源代码注释。建议先查看建议性结果，再根据扫描覆盖和质量设置策略。</p> <p><a id=\"prepare-the-workflow\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">准备工作流</h2> <p>运行扫描需要拥有 Codex Security 访问权限。添加 OpenAI API 密钥：</p> <ol> <li>在 GitHub 代码仓库中打开 <strong>Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions</strong>。</li> <li>选择 <strong>New repository secret</strong>。</li> <li>将 <code>CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY</code> 设为密钥名称，并将 OpenAI API 密钥粘贴为密钥值，然后保存。</li> </ol> <p>下面的工作流示例会自动将该密钥传递给 Codex Security Action。你不需要把 API 密钥写入工作流文件。</p> <p>只对你信任的代码仓库和拉取请求运行工作流。扫描会使用运行器的本地权限，也不会暂停等待审批。请将无关凭据和部署步骤放在单独的作业中。</p> <p><a id=\"add-the-github-actions-workflow\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"github-actions\">添加 GitHub Actions 工作流</h2> <p><strong>扫描费用：</strong>以下示例会使用你的 API 密钥，可能产生费用。两个示例都没有设置 <code>max-cost</code>，因此没有预估费用停止阈值。如要将每次扫描的阈值设为 5 美元，请在 Codex Security Action 的 <code>with</code> 配置中添加 <code>max-cost: \"5\"</code>。这不是硬性支出上限；已经开始的请求可能会使费用超过阈值。费用计价支持要求请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-cb94fa07f6e7450c?anchor=set-an-optional-scan-budget\">设置可选扫描预算</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"scan-the-repository-on-a-schedule\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_2\">按计划扫描代码仓库</h3> <p>以下工作流每周一 UTC 时间 07:23 扫描默认分支。你也可以在 GitHub 的 <strong>Actions</strong> 选项卡中手动运行。该工作流使用 x64 的 GitHub 托管 Ubuntu 24.04 运行器，并会自动配置所需的沙盒。</p> <ol> <li>在代码仓库中选择 <strong>Add file → Create new file</strong>。</li> <li>将文件命名为 <code>.github/workflows/codex-security-repository.yml</code>。</li> <li>粘贴以下工作流，并将其提交到默认分支。</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">name: Codex Security repository\n\non:\n  workflow_dispatch:\n  schedule:\n    - cron: \"23 7 * * 1\" # Mondays at 07:23 UTC\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\njobs:\n  security:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 120\n    steps:\n      - name: Set up the Ubuntu sandbox\n        run: |\n          sudo apt-get update\n          sudo apt-get install --yes bubblewrap apparmor-profiles\n          sudo apparmor_parser -r /usr/share/apparmor/extra-profiles/bwrap-userns-restrict\n\n      - name: Check out the repository\n        uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n\n      - name: Scan the repository\n        id: security\n        uses: openai/codex-security@3f61e5150981a5087c32e4395bbaa8ce5ce0c3e3 # action-v0.3.0\n        with:\n          scope: repository\n          model: gpt-6-sol\n          # For approved Daybreak Blue access, uncomment the next input.\n          # cyber-access-program: daybreak_blue\n          effort: high\n          fail-on-severity: none\n          upload-artifacts: \"true\"\n        env:\n          OPENAI_API_KEY: ${{ secrets.CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY }}\n</code></pre> <p><strong>关于版本：</strong>两个示例都将 Codex Security Action 固定在提交 <code>3f61e5150981a5087c32e4395bbaa8ce5ce0c3e3</code>，对应 <code>action-v0.3.0</code> 版本；它会安装 CLI <code>0.3.0</code>。更新固定的提交版本前，请先检查新版 Action。</p> <p><strong>关于运行器：</strong>Action 需要 Node.js 24 和 Python 3.11 或更高版本；此运行器已提供这些依赖。沙盒设置会安装 <code>bubblewrap</code> 软件包，并在扫描前加载所提供的 AppArmor 配置文件。在此运行器上，仅安装软件包还不够。</p> <p>要手动运行工作流，请打开 <strong>Actions → Codex Security repository → Run workflow</strong>。运行完成后，打开该次运行即可查看摘要、注释和可下载报告。</p> <p>由于 <code>fail-on-severity</code> 设置为 <code>none</code>，发现项只会写入报告，不会阻止作业通过。扫描器错误和必要的报告错误仍会导致作业失败。</p> <p>如要只扫描选定文件夹，请在扫描步骤的 <code>with</code> 配置中添加以换行符分隔的路径：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">paths: |\n  src/api\n  src/auth\n</code></pre> <p>路径筛选要求 <code>scope: repository</code>，且不支持展开 glob 模式。执行差异扫描时，请省略 <code>paths</code>。保留 <code>persist-credentials: false</code>，并在检出代码后立即运行扫描。</p> <p><a id=\"scan-pull-request-changes\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_3\">扫描拉取请求中的变更</h3> <p>使用同一个密钥，创建 <code>.github/workflows/codex-security-pr.yml</code>：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">name: Codex Security PR\n\non:\n  pull_request:\n    types: [opened, synchronize, reopened, ready_for_review]\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\nconcurrency:\n  group: codex-security-pr-${{ github.event.pull_request.number }}\n  cancel-in-progress: true\n\njobs:\n  security:\n    if: github.event.pull_request.head.repo.full_name == github.repository &amp;&amp; github.actor != 'dependabot[bot]'\n    name: Codex Security\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 60\n    steps:\n      - name: Set up the Ubuntu sandbox\n        run: |\n          sudo apt-get update\n          sudo apt-get install --yes bubblewrap apparmor-profiles\n          sudo apparmor_parser -r /usr/share/apparmor/extra-profiles/bwrap-userns-restrict\n\n      - name: Check out the pull request\n        uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1\n        with:\n          ref: ${{ github.event.pull_request.head.sha }}\n          fetch-depth: 0\n          persist-credentials: false\n\n      - name: Scan PR changes\n        id: security\n        uses: openai/codex-security@3f61e5150981a5087c32e4395bbaa8ce5ce0c3e3 # action-v0.3.0\n        with:\n          scope: diff\n          model: gpt-6-sol\n          # For approved Daybreak Blue access, uncomment the next input.\n          # cyber-access-program: daybreak_blue\n          effort: high\n          fail-on-severity: none\n          upload-artifacts: \"true\"\n        env:\n          OPENAI_API_KEY: ${{ secrets.CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY }}\n</code></pre> <p>从同一代码仓库中的分支创建或更新拉取请求。Action 会使用完整 Git 历史找到准确的合并基点，并扫描从该基点到检出的拉取请求提交之间的变更。在拉取请求的 <strong>Checks</strong> 中查看 <strong>Codex Security</strong> 检查。建议先查看建议性发现项；准备好将结果设为合并门槛后，再<a href=\"#/article/a-cb94fa07f6e7450c?anchor=choose-a-severity-policy\">选择严重级别策略</a>。</p> <p>此示例会跳过来自 fork 的拉取请求，以及由 <code>dependabot[bot]</code> 创建的拉取请求。被跳过的作业不代表已经完成安全审查。如要纳入这些机器人拉取请求，请删除对 actor 的排除条件，并将 <code>CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY</code> 配置为 <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/reference/supply-chain-security/troubleshoot-dependabot/dependabot-on-actions#accessing-secrets\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><code>dependabot[bot]</code> 可访问的密钥（需联网）</a>。Action 不支持 <code>pull_request_target</code> 或 <code>workflow_run</code>。</p> <p>扫描器会读取检出代码中适用的 <code>SECURITY.md</code> 指南，其中也包括拉取请求对策略文件所作的变更。请将这些变更与代码一并审查。</p> <p><a id=\"configure-optional-daybreak-access\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"daybreak\">配置可选的 Daybreak 访问权限</h3> <p>Daybreak 是可选功能。两个工作流示例都使用 <code>gpt-6-sol</code>。如果你的组织已获准使用<a href=\"#/article/a-04f6dcc4a4fe6044?anchor=trusted-access-for-cyber\">网络安全可信访问计划（Trusted Access for Cyber）</a>，请在扫描步骤的 <code>with</code> 配置中删除 <code>cyber-access-program</code> 前的 <code>#</code> 注释符：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">model: gpt-6-sol\ncyber-access-program: daybreak_blue\n</code></pre> <p>请使用来自已启用 Daybreak Blue 且有权访问 <code>gpt-6-sol</code> 的项目的 API 密钥。</p> <p>该计划输入也接受 <code>standard</code>。如果没有 Daybreak 访问权限，请使用 API 密钥在标准安全措施下有权访问的模型，并省略 <code>cyber-access-program</code> 或将其设为 <code>standard</code>。选择模型或计划名称不会授予访问权限。请参阅 Action 的 <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex-security/blob/3f61e5150981a5087c32e4395bbaa8ce5ce0c3e3/github-action/README.md#daybreak-access-and-refusals\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Daybreak 访问指南（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>如果拒绝或安全拦截导致扫描中止，Action 将失败；即使 <code>fail-on-severity</code> 设为 <code>none</code> 也一样。该输入只控制发现项策略，不控制扫描器错误。</p> <p><a id=\"set-an-optional-scan-budget\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">设置可选扫描预算</h3> <p>两个工作流示例都没有设置 <code>max-cost</code>，因此没有预估费用停止阈值。如要设置阈值，请使用 <code>max-cost</code> 输入指定一个大于零的美元金额。直接使用 CLI 扫描时，请添加 <code>--max-cost</code>。</p> <p>所选模型必须由 CLI 的价格机制支持，才能使用费用限制。预估阈值不是硬性支出上限；已经开始的请求可能会使费用超过它。</p> <p>如果扫描因达到阈值而停止，请检查发现项和 <code>coverage.json</code>。费用限制的具体行为请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=set-output-and-policy-options\">输出和策略选项</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"save-reports-and-upload-sarif\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"sarif\">保存报告并上传 SARIF</h3> <p>示例将 <code>upload-artifacts: \"true\"</code> 设为启用状态，以保存可下载报告；报告保留七天。报告可能包含源代码片段、漏洞证据和修复详情。请根据代码的敏感程度，选择合适的保留期限和代码仓库访问范围。Action 只会上传允许清单中的已验证报告；不要递归上传其 <code>results-directory</code> 输出。</p> <p>SARIF 上传是可选的。对于私有或内部代码仓库，请在上传前启用 <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/how-tos/find-and-fix-code-vulnerabilities/integrate-with-existing-tools/upload-sarif-file\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">GitHub Code Security（需联网）</a>。将工作流的 <code>permissions</code> 配置替换为：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">permissions:\n  contents: read\n  security-events: write\n  actions: read # Required for private repositories\n</code></pre> <p>然后在任一工作流的扫描步骤之后添加以下步骤：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">- name: Upload security findings\n  if: ${{ always() &amp;&amp; steps.security.outputs.sarif-upload-ready == 'true' }}\n  uses: github/codeql-action/upload-sarif@b96794f015dfd88f77b49b1c93e0fa7110f94c63 # v4.38.0\n  with:\n    sarif_file: ${{ steps.security.outputs.sarif-path }}\n    sha: ${{ steps.security.outputs.scanned-sha }}\n    ref: ${{ steps.security.outputs.analysis-ref }}\n    category: codex-security-repository\n</code></pre> <p>在拉取请求工作流中，请将 <code>category: codex-security-pr</code> 设为 PR 工作流的类别，以便为不同扫描范围使用不同类别。扫描步骤必须保留 <code>id: security</code>。即使发现项导致严重级别策略未通过，已完成且通过验证的报告仍可供上传。扫描失败或中断、差异为空、或处于试运行状态时，不会上传 SARIF。</p> <p>所有设置、状态字段和报告路径，请参阅 Action 的<a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex-security/blob/3f61e5150981a5087c32e4395bbaa8ce5ce0c3e3/github-action/README.md#inputs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">输入和输出参考（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-severity-policy\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">选择严重级别策略</h2> <p>GitHub 工作流初始设置为 <code>fail-on-severity: none</code>。如要在已完成的扫描发现高危或严重级别的问题时让作业失败，请修改扫描步骤的输入：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">fail-on-severity: high\n</code></pre> <p>在代码仓库规则中，将 <strong>Codex Security</strong> 设为必需状态检查，以便在拉取请求作业失败时阻止合并。即使是必需检查，GitHub 也会将<a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/pull-requests/how-tos/merge-and-close-pull-requests/troubleshooting-required-status-checks#handling-skipped-but-required-checks\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">有条件跳过的作业视为成功（需联网）</a>。fork 拉取请求和由 <code>dependabot[bot]</code> 创建的拉取请求会在未扫描的情况下通过此检查。若要阻止这些跳过的情况，请<a href=\"#/article/a-cb94fa07f6e7450c?anchor=require-a-successful-completed-scan\">要求扫描成功且已完成</a>。</p> <p>Action 会根据 CLI 的结果报告扫描状态：</p> <ul> <li>退出代码 <code>0</code>：将 <code>scan-status: completed</code> 设为已完成，并将 <code>policy-status: passed</code> 设为通过。</li> <li>退出代码 <code>1</code>：将 <code>scan-status: completed</code> 设为已完成，并将 <code>policy-status: failed</code> 设为失败；若发现项达到或超过配置的严重级别，步骤会失败。</li> <li>退出代码 <code>2</code> 或进程被中断：将 <code>scan-status: failed</code> 设为失败，并将 <code>policy-status: not-evaluated</code> 设为未评估；步骤会失败。</li> <li>必需报告无效或缺失、检出的代码发生变化、请求的产物上传失败，以及运行时清理失败，也都会导致步骤失败。</li> </ul> <p>扫描已完成表示所配置的分析已生成有效结果。<code>coverage.json</code> 中的范围排除项、延期调查和其他说明不会形成单独的扫描结果，也不会绕过严重级别策略。扫描完成并不表示已经发现所有漏洞；评估结果时请检查 <code>coverage.json</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"require-a-successful-completed-scan\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">要求扫描成功且已完成</h3> <p>如要采用更严格的策略，请添加一个独立的门禁作业，即使扫描作业失败或被 GitHub 跳过，该门禁仍会运行。扫描作业内的步骤无法检查被跳过的作业，因为该作业中的任何步骤都不会运行。</p> <p>在拉取请求工作流中，给现有的 <code>security</code> 作业添加以下 <code>outputs</code> 映射；缩进层级应与 <code>runs-on</code> 和 <code>steps</code> 相同：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">outputs:\n  scan-status: ${{ steps.security.outputs.scan-status }}\n</code></pre> <p>然后在 <code>jobs</code> 下与现有 <code>security</code> 作业并列，添加以下作业：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">security-gate:\n  name: Codex Security gate\n  needs: security\n  if: ${{ always() }}\n  runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n  steps:\n    - name: Require a successful, completed scan\n      env:\n        SCAN_RESULT: ${{ needs.security.result }}\n        SCAN_STATUS: ${{ needs.security.outputs.scan-status }}\n      run: test \"$SCAN_RESULT\" = success &amp;&amp; test \"$SCAN_STATUS\" = completed\n</code></pre> <p>将 <strong>Codex Security gate</strong> 设为此策略的必需状态检查。它要求扫描作业成功，并且 <code>scan-status: completed</code>。同时检查这两项，可以保留严重级别策略、报告和清理流程所产生的失败状态，即使扫描本身已经完成。</p> <p>根据示例中的排除条件，此门禁会阻止 fork 拉取请求和来自 <code>dependabot[bot]</code> 的拉取请求。它也会阻止差异为空和试运行的情况，因为 Action 会将这些情况标记为 <code>skipped</code>。门禁本身不会扫描被排除的拉取请求；只有在这些情况确实应阻止合并时，才采用此策略。</p> <p><a id=\"troubleshoot-a-scan\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">扫描故障排查</h2> <ul> <li><strong>未知 Git 引用或差异不符合预期：</strong>使用 <code>fetch-depth: 0</code> 检出拉取请求分支。</li> <li><strong>沙盒启动错误：</strong>在 Ubuntu 24.04 上，需在 Action 运行前安装 <code>bubblewrap</code> 软件包并加载 AppArmor 配置文件。仅安装软件包不会加载所需配置。</li> <li><strong>缺少凭据：</strong>确认受信任的工作流可以读取 <code>CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY</code>，并将其映射到扫描步骤的 <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code> 环境变量。</li> <li><strong>Python 设置错误：</strong>Action 要求 Python 3.11 或更高版本。</li> <li><strong>覆盖说明：</strong>检查 <code>coverage.json</code> 中的范围排除项和延期调查。这些说明不会导致执行失败，也不会绕过严重级别策略。</li> <li><strong>缺少 SARIF：</strong>检查 <code>scan-status</code>、<code>report-status</code> 和 <code>sarif-upload-ready</code>。如果可选 SARIF 缺失，Action 会发出警告，但不会更改扫描结果；请求的产物上传失败仍会导致作业失败。</li> <li><strong>SARIF 上传错误：</strong>确认组织已为该代码仓库启用 GitHub Code Security，并且工作流已授予 <code>actions: read</code>、<code>contents: read</code> 和 <code>security-events: write</code> 权限。</li> </ul> <p>命令、标志、产物和输出字段详见 <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34\">CLI 参考</a>。其他 CI 提供商请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-8d926b82884d5f99\">CI/CD 概览</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"run-codex-security-in-github-actions\">Run Codex Security in GitHub Actions</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Run Codex Security in GitHub Actions to review pull-request changes or scan your repository on a schedule. The Action installs the CLI, saves structured reports, and adds a job summary and source annotations. Start with advisory results, then configure enforcement after reviewing coverage and scan quality.</p> <h2 id=\"prepare-the-workflow\">Prepare the workflow</h2> <p>Running scans requires Codex Security access. To add your OpenAI API key:</p> <ol> <li>In your GitHub repository, open <strong>Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions</strong>.</li> <li>Select <strong>New repository secret</strong>.</li> <li>Enter <code>CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY</code> as the name and paste your OpenAI API key as the value. Save the secret.</li> </ol> <p>The workflow examples below pass this secret to the Codex Security Action automatically. You don't need to put your API key in the workflow file.</p> <p>Run the workflow only for repositories and pull requests you trust. Scans use the runner's local permissions and don't pause for approval. Keep unrelated credentials and deployment steps in separate jobs.</p> <h2 id=\"add-the-github-actions-workflow\">Add the GitHub Actions workflow</h2> <p><strong>Scan costs:</strong> These workflows use your API key and may incur charges. Both examples omit <code>max-cost</code>, so they have no estimated cost stop threshold. To set a threshold of $5 per scan, add <code>max-cost: \"5\"</code> to the Codex Security Action's <code>with</code> settings. This isn't a hard spending cap: requests already in progress can exceed it. See <a href=\"#/article/a-cb94fa07f6e7450c?anchor=set-an-optional-scan-budget\">Set an optional scan budget</a> for pricing-support requirements.</p> <h3 id=\"scan-the-repository-on-a-schedule\">Scan the repository on a schedule</h3> <p>The workflow below scans your default branch every Monday at 07:23 UTC. You can also run it manually from GitHub's <strong>Actions</strong> tab. It uses an x64 GitHub-hosted Ubuntu 24.04 runner and sets up the required sandbox automatically.</p> <ol> <li>In your repository, select <strong>Add file → Create new file</strong>.</li> <li>Name the file <code>.github/workflows/codex-security-repository.yml</code>.</li> <li>Paste the workflow below and commit it to your default branch.</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">name: Codex Security repository\n\non:\n  workflow_dispatch:\n  schedule:\n    - cron: \"23 7 * * 1\" # Mondays at 07:23 UTC\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\njobs:\n  security:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 120\n    steps:\n      - name: Set up the Ubuntu sandbox\n        run: |\n          sudo apt-get update\n          sudo apt-get install --yes bubblewrap apparmor-profiles\n          sudo apparmor_parser -r /usr/share/apparmor/extra-profiles/bwrap-userns-restrict\n\n      - name: Check out the repository\n        uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n\n      - name: Scan the repository\n        id: security\n        uses: openai/codex-security@3f61e5150981a5087c32e4395bbaa8ce5ce0c3e3 # action-v0.3.0\n        with:\n          scope: repository\n          model: gpt-6-sol\n          # For approved Daybreak Blue access, uncomment the next input.\n          # cyber-access-program: daybreak_blue\n          effort: high\n          fail-on-severity: none\n          upload-artifacts: \"true\"\n        env:\n          OPENAI_API_KEY: ${{ secrets.CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY }}\n</code></pre> <p><strong>About the version:</strong> Both examples pin the Codex Security Action to commit <code>3f61e5150981a5087c32e4395bbaa8ce5ce0c3e3</code> for the <code>action-v0.3.0</code> release, which installs CLI <code>0.3.0</code>. Review a newer Action release before updating the pinned commit.</p> <p><strong>Adapting the runner:</strong> The Action needs Node.js 24 and Python 3.11 or later, which this runner provides. The sandbox setup installs the <code>bubblewrap</code> package and loads the supplied AppArmor profile before the scan. Installing the package alone is not enough on this runner.</p> <p>To run the workflow manually, open <strong>Actions → Codex Security repository → Run workflow</strong>. Open a completed run to review the summary, annotations, and downloadable reports.</p> <p>Findings are report-only because <code>fail-on-severity</code> is <code>none</code>. Scanner and required reporting errors still fail the job.</p> <p>To scan selected folders, add newline-separated literal paths to the scan step's <code>with</code> block:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">paths: |\n  src/api\n  src/auth\n</code></pre> <p>Paths require <code>scope: repository</code> and do not expand globs. For diff scans, omit <code>paths</code>. Keep <code>persist-credentials: false</code> and run the scan immediately after checkout.</p> <h3 id=\"scan-pull-request-changes\">Scan pull-request changes</h3> <p>Using the same secret, create <code>.github/workflows/codex-security-pr.yml</code>:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">name: Codex Security PR\n\non:\n  pull_request:\n    types: [opened, synchronize, reopened, ready_for_review]\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\nconcurrency:\n  group: codex-security-pr-${{ github.event.pull_request.number }}\n  cancel-in-progress: true\n\njobs:\n  security:\n    if: github.event.pull_request.head.repo.full_name == github.repository &amp;&amp; github.actor != 'dependabot[bot]'\n    name: Codex Security\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 60\n    steps:\n      - name: Set up the Ubuntu sandbox\n        run: |\n          sudo apt-get update\n          sudo apt-get install --yes bubblewrap apparmor-profiles\n          sudo apparmor_parser -r /usr/share/apparmor/extra-profiles/bwrap-userns-restrict\n\n      - name: Check out the pull request\n        uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1\n        with:\n          ref: ${{ github.event.pull_request.head.sha }}\n          fetch-depth: 0\n          persist-credentials: false\n\n      - name: Scan PR changes\n        id: security\n        uses: openai/codex-security@3f61e5150981a5087c32e4395bbaa8ce5ce0c3e3 # action-v0.3.0\n        with:\n          scope: diff\n          model: gpt-6-sol\n          # For approved Daybreak Blue access, uncomment the next input.\n          # cyber-access-program: daybreak_blue\n          effort: high\n          fail-on-severity: none\n          upload-artifacts: \"true\"\n        env:\n          OPENAI_API_KEY: ${{ secrets.CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY }}\n</code></pre> <p>Open or update a PR from a branch in the same repository. The Action uses the full history to find the exact merge base and scans changes through the checked-out PR head. View the <strong>Codex Security</strong> check under <strong>Checks</strong> in the PR. Start with advisory findings, then <a href=\"#/article/a-cb94fa07f6e7450c?anchor=choose-a-severity-policy\">choose a severity policy</a> when you are ready to gate changes.</p> <p>This example skips fork PRs and PRs opened by <code>dependabot[bot]</code>. A skipped job is not evidence of a security review. To include these bot PRs, remove the actor exclusion and also configure <code>CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY</code> as a <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/reference/supply-chain-security/troubleshoot-dependabot/dependabot-on-actions#accessing-secrets\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">secret for <code>dependabot[bot]</code> (online)</a>. The Action does not support <code>pull_request_target</code> or <code>workflow_run</code>.</p> <p>The scanner reads applicable <code>SECURITY.md</code> guidance from the checkout, including policy changes in the PR. Review those changes alongside the code.</p> <h3 id=\"configure-optional-daybreak-access\">Configure optional Daybreak access</h3> <p>Daybreak is optional. Both workflow examples use <code>gpt-6-sol</code>. If your organization has been approved for <a href=\"#/article/a-04f6dcc4a4fe6044?anchor=trusted-access-for-cyber\">Trusted Access for Cyber</a>, remove the <code>#</code> before <code>cyber-access-program</code> in the scan step's <code>with</code> block:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">model: gpt-6-sol\ncyber-access-program: daybreak_blue\n</code></pre> <p>Use an API key from a project enabled for Daybreak Blue with access to <code>gpt-6-sol</code>.</p> <p>The program input also accepts <code>standard</code>. Without Daybreak access, use a model your API key can access under standard safeguards and omit <code>cyber-access-program</code> or set it to <code>standard</code>. Selecting a model or program does not grant access. See the Action's <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex-security/blob/3f61e5150981a5087c32e4395bbaa8ce5ce0c3e3/github-action/README.md#daybreak-access-and-refusals\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Daybreak access guidance (online)</a>.</p> <p>A refusal or safety block that aborts the scan fails the Action, including when <code>fail-on-severity</code> is <code>none</code>. That input controls findings policy, not scanner errors.</p> <h3 id=\"set-an-optional-scan-budget\">Set an optional scan budget</h3> <p>Both workflow examples omit <code>max-cost</code>, so they have no estimated cost stop threshold. To set one, add a positive USD amount with the <code>max-cost</code> input. For direct CLI scans, use <code>--max-cost</code>.</p> <p>The cost limit requires CLI pricing support for the selected model. The estimated threshold is not a hard spending cap: the cost of requests already in progress can exceed it. Review findings and <code>coverage.json</code> if a scan stops at the threshold. See <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=set-output-and-policy-options\">output and policy options</a> for cost-limit behavior.</p> <h3 id=\"save-reports-and-upload-sarif\">Save reports and upload SARIF</h3> <p>The examples set <code>upload-artifacts: \"true\"</code> to save downloadable reports with a seven-day retention window. Reports can contain source snippets, vulnerability evidence, and remediation details. Choose a retention window and repository access appropriate for your code. The Action uploads only validated reports on its allowlist; do not recursively upload its <code>results-directory</code> output.</p> <p>SARIF upload is optional. For private or internal repositories, enable <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/how-tos/find-and-fix-code-vulnerabilities/integrate-with-existing-tools/upload-sarif-file\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">GitHub Code Security (online)</a> before uploading. Replace the workflow's <code>permissions</code> block with:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">permissions:\n  contents: read\n  security-events: write\n  actions: read # Required for private repositories\n</code></pre> <p>Then add this step after the scan in either workflow:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">- name: Upload security findings\n  if: ${{ always() &amp;&amp; steps.security.outputs.sarif-upload-ready == 'true' }}\n  uses: github/codeql-action/upload-sarif@b96794f015dfd88f77b49b1c93e0fa7110f94c63 # v4.38.0\n  with:\n    sarif_file: ${{ steps.security.outputs.sarif-path }}\n    sha: ${{ steps.security.outputs.scanned-sha }}\n    ref: ${{ steps.security.outputs.analysis-ref }}\n    category: codex-security-repository\n</code></pre> <p>For the PR workflow, use <code>category: codex-security-pr</code> so each scope has a distinct category. Keep <code>id: security</code> on the scan step. Complete, validated reports remain available for upload when findings fail the severity policy. SARIF is not uploaded for failed or interrupted scans, empty diffs, or dry runs.</p> <p>See the Action's <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex-security/blob/3f61e5150981a5087c32e4395bbaa8ce5ce0c3e3/github-action/README.md#inputs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">input and output reference (online)</a> for all settings, status fields, and report paths.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-a-severity-policy\">Choose a severity policy</h2> <p>The GitHub workflows start with <code>fail-on-severity: none</code>. To fail on high or critical findings from a completed scan, change the scan step's input:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">fail-on-severity: high\n</code></pre> <p>Make <strong>Codex Security</strong> a required status check in your repository rules to block merges when the PR job fails. GitHub treats a <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/pull-requests/how-tos/merge-and-close-pull-requests/troubleshooting-required-status-checks#handling-skipped-but-required-checks\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">conditionally skipped job as successful (online)</a>, even for required checks. Fork PRs and PRs from <code>dependabot[bot]</code> pass this check without a scan. To block those skips, <a href=\"#/article/a-cb94fa07f6e7450c?anchor=require-a-successful-completed-scan\">require a successful, completed scan</a>.</p> <p>The Action follows the CLI outcome:</p> <ul> <li>Exit code <code>0</code> sets <code>scan-status: completed</code> and <code>policy-status: passed</code>.</li> <li>Exit code <code>1</code> sets <code>scan-status: completed</code> and <code>policy-status: failed</code>; the step fails on findings at or above the configured severity.</li> <li>Exit code <code>2</code> or an interrupted process sets <code>scan-status: failed</code> and <code>policy-status: not-evaluated</code>; the step fails.</li> <li>Invalid or missing required reports, a changed checkout, failures to upload requested artifacts, and runtime cleanup failures also fail the step.</li> </ul> <p>A completed scan means the configured analysis produced a valid result. Scope exclusions, deferred investigations, and other notes in <code>coverage.json</code> do not create a separate scan outcome or bypass the severity policy. Completion does not certify that every vulnerability was found. Review <code>coverage.json</code> when assessing the result.</p> <h3 id=\"require-a-successful-completed-scan\">Require a successful, completed scan</h3> <p>For a stricter policy, add a separate gate that runs even if the scan job fails or GitHub skips it. A step inside the scan job can't check a skipped job because none of its steps run.</p> <p>In the PR workflow, add this <code>outputs</code> mapping to the existing <code>security</code> job, at the same indentation as <code>runs-on</code> and <code>steps</code>:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">outputs:\n  scan-status: ${{ steps.security.outputs.scan-status }}\n</code></pre> <p>Then add this job under <code>jobs</code>, alongside the existing <code>security</code> job:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">security-gate:\n  name: Codex Security gate\n  needs: security\n  if: ${{ always() }}\n  runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n  steps:\n    - name: Require a successful, completed scan\n      env:\n        SCAN_RESULT: ${{ needs.security.result }}\n        SCAN_STATUS: ${{ needs.security.outputs.scan-status }}\n      run: test \"$SCAN_RESULT\" = success &amp;&amp; test \"$SCAN_STATUS\" = completed\n</code></pre> <p>Make <strong>Codex Security gate</strong> the required status check for this policy. It requires both a successful scan job and <code>scan-status: completed</code>. Checking both preserves failures from the severity policy, reporting, and cleanup, even when the scan itself completed.</p> <p>With the example's exclusions, this gate blocks fork PRs and PRs from <code>dependabot[bot]</code>. It also blocks empty diffs and dry runs, which the Action marks as <code>skipped</code>. The gate doesn't scan excluded PRs. Choose this policy only if these cases should prevent merging.</p> <h2 id=\"troubleshoot-a-scan\">Troubleshoot a scan</h2> <ul> <li><strong>Unknown Git ref or unexpected diff:</strong> Check out the PR head with <code>fetch-depth: 0</code>.</li> <li><strong>Sandbox startup error:</strong> On Ubuntu 24.04, install the <code>bubblewrap</code> package and load the AppArmor profile before the Action. Installing the package alone does not load the required profile.</li> <li><strong>Missing credentials:</strong> Confirm that <code>CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY</code> is available to the trusted workflow and mapped to the scan step's <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code> environment variable.</li> <li><strong>Python setup error:</strong> The Action requires Python 3.11 or later.</li> <li><strong>Coverage notes:</strong> Review scope exclusions and deferred investigations in <code>coverage.json</code>. These notes do not cause execution failures or bypass the severity policy.</li> <li><strong>Missing SARIF:</strong> Inspect <code>scan-status</code>, <code>report-status</code>, and <code>sarif-upload-ready</code>. If optional SARIF is missing, the Action warns without changing the scan outcome; requested artifact-upload failures still fail the job.</li> <li><strong>SARIF upload error:</strong> Confirm that your organization has enabled GitHub Code Security for the repository and that the workflow grants <code>actions: read</code>, <code>contents: read</code>, and <code>security-events: write</code>.</li> </ul> <p>For every command, flag, artifact, and output field, see the <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34\">CLI reference</a>. For other providers, see the <a href=\"#/article/a-8d926b82884d5f99\">CI/CD overview</a>.</p>"};
